      "content": "Global governance, as exemplified by the UN, is inherently flawed because it prioritizes the interests of powerful nations over smaller ones. This imbalance undermines the very concept of national sovereignty and independence. The UN's structure and decision-making processes often reflect the dominance of major powers, making it difficult for smaller countries to have their voices heard and their interests protected. In essence, global governance can only work if it genuinely respects and upholds the sovereignty of all nations, which is currently not the case. Therefore, it poses a significant threat to the independence of nation-states and cannot be considered a viable solution for true global cooperation.",
